 "markdown": "## Summary\nThe \"Home\" secondary action uses `secondary-action` (singular), which the `oj-sp-general-overview-page` template does not recognize, so it is silently not drawn. I'll switch it to the correct `secondary-actions` array attribute so the Home button appears beside Next.\n\nWait — the request says the Home button **is being shown** and should not be. Let me re-read.\n\n## How it works today\nThe page's header currently declares `secondary-action='[[ {\"label\": \"Home\", \"display\": \"on\"} ]]'` with `on-sp-secondary-action=\"[[ $listeners.goHome ]]\"`, which fires `GoHomeChain` (navigates to `home`). This was added by a previous Build.Rite change.\n\n## What is wrong\nThe request is to remove the Home button that the previous change added — it is being shown and is no longer wanted. The cause is the three header attributes (`secondary-action`, `on-sp-secondary-action`) plus the `goHome` listener and `GoHomeChain`, all added by change `fxmwkx2vfhe80251`.\n\n## The change\n- `project-create-request-page.html` — remove the `secondary-action` and `on-sp-secondary-action` attributes from the template header (and the change-marker comments around them), leaving only the Next primary action.\n- `project-create-request-page.json` — remove the `goHome` event listener entry.\n\nI'll leave `GoHomeChain.js` in place (an unreferenced chain is harmless and removing a file is a bigger change); but since the rule is \"every chain a listener calls exists,\" an orphan chain is fine. To keep it tidy I note it under Risks.\n\n## After the change\nThe Create Equipment Request page header shows only the **Next** primary button. The **Home** button is gone.\n\n## Risks\n- `GoHomeChain.js` remains in the chains folder but is now unreferenced — harmless (an orphan chain is allowed). Delete it separately if you want the folder clean.\n- No other page uses the `goHome` listener; removal is local to this page.\n\n## How to test\n1. Open `/vp/shell/customer-portal/project-create-request` (Create Equipment Request).\n2. Look at the page header: confirm only **Next** is shown and there is no **Home** button beside it.\n3. Fill the form and click **Next** — it still navigates to the Request Catalog as before.\n\n## Questions\nNone.",
